  "origin": "floor centre at the foot of the bark; the bark is a vertical wall whose face is the plane y = 0.03, with its relief toward -y and the open air in front of it. Gravity runs -z, down the screen. The god camera hovers in the air at -y and looks along +y straight at the bark, so 'top-down' here means straight onto the bark, which is the ground of the view. Real metres at human scale: the people are 2 mm tall. Three terraces from z 0.165 to 0.24 hold the city; the Long Crack runs down the grooves below it; Splinterwatch is beside it to the east (+x).",
